      "name": "perl-Try-Tiny",
      "epoch": "0",
      "version": "0.30",
      "release": "13.el9",
      "architecture": "noarch",
      "summary": "Minimal try/catch with proper localization of $@",
      "description": "This module provides bare bones try/catch statements that are designed to\nminimize common mistakes with eval blocks, and NOTHING else.\n\nThis is unlike TryCatch, which provides a nice syntax and avoids adding\nanother call stack layer, and supports calling return from the try block to\nreturn from the parent subroutine. These extra features come at a cost of a\nfew dependencies, namely Devel::Declare and Scope::Upper that are occasionally\nproblematic, and the additional catch filtering uses Moose type constraints,\nwhich may not be desirable either.",
      "homepage": "https://metacpan.org/release/Try-Tiny",
